        "action": "fill",
        "value": "I have two ongoing commitments outside of school. I co-founded Open Health Intelligence, where I am the technical lead for ClarityAtlas, an iOS health product built with Swift, SwiftUI, Supabase, and Apple health and motion data. I built the passive sleep-estimation system that uses HealthKit and Core Motion signals like step count and gait speed instead of requiring a wearable, and we shipped it into a live Hopkins pilot with 30+ users. I also work on applied machine learning and product at Summer Atlantic Capital / SAC Nexus, where I own much of the ML core of an anomaly-detection and alert-prioritization system, including the event-ingestion pipeline, a versioned FastAPI detection service, temporal sequence models over event streams, and a retrieval-augmented explanation layer for analysts. Neither is a data resilience or data security posture product, so I do not see a commercial or product conflict with Veeam. The closest technical adjacency is anomaly detection over event streams, and I am happy to discuss boundaries before starting.",
